Building Orientation:
Physical Orientation: Where you find yourself in your surroundings (Learn about your surroundings first before placing yourself)
Mental Orientation: Attention to things beyond your eyes. I.e. Days, dates etc.
Intellectual Orientation: combination of the above (situational orientation). Aware of both the seen and unseen environments. Act with as much power/thinking as is needed for the situation.
Basically understanding where you are in your place, who can take what situation is provided. (determines how you approach learning, problems, and information. It is less about how much you already know and more about whether your mind is directed toward curiosity, questioning, evidence, and understanding.)
I.e. What exactly does it do? What assumptions am I making? What evidence supports the conclusion? Could there be a legitimate explanation? What evidence would prove me wrong? 
