Building Comprehension:
The big overall picture to grasp
Taking hold of something mentally in order to grasp it (Totality you are going for)
Seeing the picture on the box so you know how those pieces connect 
I.e. as per https://gemini.google.com/app/7c0ed35e777b2490
If you aim for totality as a founder, you try to track 50 different metrics, read every market report, and satisfy every user feature request. You end up drowned in data without knowing where the business is actually heading.
If you have comprehension, you might only look at 3 key metrics—for instance, customer retention, acquisition cost, and burn rate—and instantly understand:
"Our marketing is bringing people in, but they're dropping off after week two because our onboarding flow is too complex. If we fix onboarding, our unit economics instantly work."
That insight isn't about knowing everything (totality); it's about understanding how the critical pieces fit together and affect one another (comprehension).
It's moving from "I have a bunch of pieces" (Totality) to "I get how they work together." 
why and how something fits in so you know exactly when to refer/use it.

